ketch; the fence IS the integration. NO interactive session needed or scheduled -- nothing waits on Nacho (relay 0007 cutover, D-011). Original text preserved below.]\n\nReview the prototype script at /root/personalization/bin/context_budget.sh and the tool-call layer (especially iar-tool-call.el and iar-request-watchdog.el) to plan how to integrate the context budget rule into the Emacs configuration.\n\nThe integration should:\n- Track tool calls per cycle (similar to the prototype script)\n- Exit with a specific code (e.g., 1) when the threshold (200 tool calls ~ 400 msgs) is exceeded\n- Be implemented in the tool-call layer or cycle guard (iar-agent-cycle.el) without breaking existing functionality.\n\nThis integration is to be done in an interactive session with Nacho, as it requires modifying .el files.\n[t+02:24/60:00 c13/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_0b4bf6ik","function":{"index":0,"name":"list_directory","arguments":{"path":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:49:43] ROADMAP.org\nSTATE.md\nbare-repo-root-push-fixes.org\nbreaker-grace-compliance.org\nfailure-reduction/\ninteractive-bundle-nacho/\n[t+02:29/60:00 c14/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_38b4ljk1","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_knowledge","arguments":{"path":"knowledge/iar/token-burn-audit.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:50:02] Knowledge base entry not found: knowledge/iar/token-burn-audit.md\n[t+02:48/60:00 c15/300]"}]
